CITIML TO DATA CATALOG INTEGRATION – POC

1. REQUIREMENT

Rajat asked us to take three nodes from a CitiML
XPath, publish them to Data Catalog and create
parent-child relationships.


2. BASIC UNDERSTANDING

Dictionary : Container holding collections.
Concept    : Collection inside a dictionary.
Attribute  : Field inside a collection.
Node       : Individual element in CitiML XPath.
Symlink    : Relationship between metadata objects.
Lineage    : Connection between source and target.

MetaManager : UI to manage and verify metadata.
Swagger     : API documentation.
SoapUI      : Tool to execute REST API requests.
Data Catalog: Platform storing the metadata.


3. FLAT STRUCTURE VS HIERARCHY

Original CitiML hierarchy:

TradeNotification
    └── NotificationBundleDetails
          └── Events

Current flat Data Catalog structure:

CitiMLTest
    ├── TradeNotification
    ├── NotificationBundleDetails
    └── Events

All three collections exist at the same level.

To represent the original hierarchy, we create
parent-child relationships between their attributes.


